/-!
# The fibre input of Stacks 063W

Let `A → B` be smooth, let `A → C` be syntomic, let `φ : B → C` be a surjection of `A`-algebras
with kernel `I`, and let `q` be a prime of `B` containing `I`, lying over the prime `p` of `A`.
Write `T = B_q` and `R = T/pT` for the local ring of the fibre of `B` over `κ(p)` at `q`.  Then
`I R` is generated by a regular sequence of `R`, and such a sequence may be taken to be the image
of a family `f_1, …, f_r ∈ I`.

This is the input that Stacks 063W needs at the point `q`:  the two spreading-out statements
`Stacks.RingTheory.SpreadingOut.exists_notMem_isWeaklyRegular_and_flat_quotient_away` and
`Stacks.RingTheory.SpreadingOut.exists_notMem_map_eq_map_away` each carry a hypothesis on the
fibre, and the conclusion here is exactly the conjunction of those two hypotheses.

## Main results

* `Stacks.RingTheory.SpreadingOut.exists_isRegular_fibre_of_smooth_of_syntomic`:  the family
  `f_1, …, f_r ∈ I ∩ q` whose image in `B_q/pB_q` is a regular sequence generating `I B_q/pB_q`.

## Implementation notes

The mathematics is Stacks 00SF applied to the surjection `R → R/IR`.

* `R` is a regular local ring because `A → B` is smooth:  the fibre `κ(p) ⊗_A B` is a regular
  ring (Stacks 00TT and 07NF, `Algebra.isRegularRing_of_smooth`), and `R` is one of its local
  rings by `Ideal.Fiber.localizationAlgEquivQuotient`.
* `R/IR` is a complete intersection over `κ(p)` because `B/I ≅ C` is syntomic over `A`.  The
  fibre of `B/I` at the prime `q'` corresponding to `q` is a complete intersection over `κ(p)`
  (`Algebra.Syntomic.flat_localization_and_isCompleteIntersection_fiber`, Stacks 00SY through
  Stacks 00SH), and `T/IT` is an abstract localization of `B/I` at `q'`, so
  `Stacks.SyntomicLocus.isCompleteIntersection_closedFibre_iff` computes that fibre as the closed
  fibre `κ(P) ⊗_P (T/IT)` of `P = A_p → T/IT`;  then
  `Algebra.TensorProduct.quotIdealMapEquivQuotTensor` and `DoubleQuot.quotQuotEquivCommₐ` rewrite
  the latter as `(T/𝔪_P T)/I(T/𝔪_P T)`, both being `T/(IT + 𝔪_P T)`.
* Stacks 00SF (`IsCompleteIntersection.tfae`, second item) applied to `R → R/IR` then produces a
  regular sequence generating `I R`.

Two bookkeeping points dominate the formalization.

*The ideal `pT` versus `𝔪_P T`.*  Every Mathlib instance about the fibre of a quotient — the
`κ(P)`-algebra structure on `T/𝔪_P T` and its essential finite type — is stated for the ideal
`𝔪_P T`, while the statement wanted downstream speaks of `pT`.  The two agree
(`Stacks.RingTheory.SpreadingOut.map_maximalIdeal_eq_map_of_isLocalization`), but the equality is
between ideals appearing in a quotient *type*, so it is passed as a hypothesis and substituted:
that is what the ideal argument of `isRegularLocalRing_quotient_of_smooth` and the equation
argument of `exists_isRegular_ofList_eq_map_of_ideal_eq` are for.

*The regular sequence is lifted only up to units.*  The map `B → R` is not surjective, but every
element of `R` becomes the image of an element of `B` after multiplication by the image of some
`s ∉ q`, which is a unit of `R`;  this is `exists_mem_of_mem_map`, proved by induction over the
span defining `I R`.  Regularity and the generated ideal are insensitive to unit multiples
(`isRegular_of_forall₂_unit_mul`), so the lifted family serves as well as the sequence produced
by 00SF.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.22.8 (Tag 063W)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063W)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 37.24.4 (Tag 067T)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/067T)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 10.135.6 (Tag 00SF)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00SF)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 10.135.3 (Tag 00SH)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00SH)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 10.138.3 (Tag 07NF)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07NF)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 10.114.1 (Tag 00TT)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00TT)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 37.22.2 (Tag 01UG)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01UG)
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Stacks.RingTheory.SpreadingOut

open RingTheory.Sequence IsLocalRing

open scoped TensorProduct Pointwise

universe u

/-! ### Regular sequences up to unit multiples -/

section UnitMul

/-- Replacing every member of a list by a unit multiple does not change the ideal it generates. -/
private alias ofList_eq_of_forall₂_unit_mul :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ofList_eq_of_forall₂_unit_mul

/-- **Weak regularity only depends on a sequence up to unit multiples.**  This is what lets the
sequence produced in the fibre `B_q/pB_q`, whose members have denominators, be replaced by the
image of a family of elements of `B` itself. -/
private alias isWeaklyRegular_of_forall₂_unit_mul :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isWeaklyRegular_of_forall₂_unit_mul

/-- Regularity only depends on a sequence up to unit multiples. -/
private alias isRegular_of_forall₂_unit_mul :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isRegular_of_forall₂_unit_mul

/-- **Regularity of a sequence is unchanged by pushing it into a larger acting ring.**  The
`IsRegular` counterpart of `RingTheory.Sequence.isWeaklyRegular_map_algebraMap_iff`. -/
private alias isRegular_map_algebraMap_iff := Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isRegular_map_algebraMap_iff

end UnitMul

/-! ### Membership in a quotient, and lifting from the fibre -/

/-- **Lifting from the fibre to `B`, up to a unit.**  If every element of `R` becomes the image of
an element of `B` after multiplication by the image of an element of `q.primeCompl`, then every
element of `I R` becomes the image of an element of `I`. -/
private lemma exists_mem_of_mem_map {B R : Type*} [CommRing B] [CommRing R] [Algebra B R]
    (q : Ideal B) [q.IsPrime] (I : Ideal B)
    (hfrac : ∀ c : R, ∃ s ∈ q.primeCompl, ∃ b : B, algebraMap B R s * c = algebraMap B R b)
    {x : R} (hx : x ∈ I.map (algebraMap B R)) :
    ∃ s ∈ q.primeCompl, ∃ b ∈ I, algebraMap B R b = algebraMap B R s * x := by
  rw [Ideal.map, Ideal.span] at hx
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem y hy =>
    obtain ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩ := hy
    exact ⟨1, q.primeCompl.one_mem, b, hb, by rw [map_one, one_mul]⟩
  | zero => exact ⟨1, q.primeCompl.one_mem, 0, I.zero_mem, by simp⟩
  | add y z _ _ hy hz =>
    obtain ⟨s₁, hs₁, b₁, hb₁, h₁⟩ := hy
    obtain ⟨s₂, hs₂, b₂, hb₂, h₂⟩ := hz
    refine ⟨s₁ * s₂, q.primeCompl.mul_mem hs₁ hs₂, s₂ * b₁ + s₁ * b₂,
      I.add_mem (I.mul_mem_left _ hb₁) (I.mul_mem_left _ hb₂), ?_⟩
    rw [map_add, map_mul, map_mul, map_mul, h₁, h₂]
    ring
  | smul c y _ hy =>
    obtain ⟨s, hs, b, hb, h⟩ := hy
    obtain ⟨t, ht, d, hd⟩ := hfrac c
    refine ⟨t * s, q.primeCompl.mul_mem ht hs, d * b, I.mul_mem_left _ hb, ?_⟩
    rw [map_mul, map_mul, h, smul_eq_mul, ← hd]
    ring

/-! ### The fibre of a smooth algebra is a regular local ring -/

/-- **The local ring of the fibre of a smooth algebra is regular.**  Stacks 00TT and 07NF:  the
fibre `κ(p) ⊗_A B` of a smooth algebra is a regular ring, and `B_q/pB_q` is one of its local
rings.  The ideal is an independent parameter so that the equality `pB_q = 𝔪_{A_p} B_q` may be
substituted at the call site. -/
private lemma isRegularLocalRing_quotient_of_smooth {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [Algebra A B] [Algebra.Smooth A B] (p : Ideal A) [p.IsPrime] (q : Ideal B) [q.IsPrime]
    (hpq : q.comap (algebraMap A B) = p) (K : Ideal (Localization.AtPrime q))
    (hK : p.map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q)) = K) :
    IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime q ⧸ K) := by
  subst hK
  obtain ⟨Q, hQp, hQ⟩ := Ideal.Fiber.exists_comap_includeRight_eq q p hpq
  have := hQp
  subst hQ
  have : IsRegularRing (p.Fiber B) := Algebra.isRegularRing_of_smooth p.ResidueField (p.Fiber B)
  let _ := Localization.AtPrime.algebraOfLiesOver p
    (Q.comap (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : B →ₐ[A] p.Fiber B))
  exact IsRegularLocalRing.of_ringEquiv (Ideal.Fiber.localizationAlgEquivQuotient p Q).toRingEquiv

/-- The image of an extended ideal in a quotient of the extension is the ideal extended directly
to the quotient. -/
private lemma map_map_mk_eq_map {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]
    (J : Ideal R) (K : Ideal S) :
    (J.map (algebraMap R S)).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk K) = J.map (algebraMap R (S ⧸ K)) := by
  rw [Ideal.map_map]
  rfl

/-! ### Upgrading an isomorphism to the residue field -/

/-- A `P`-algebra isomorphism between two `κ(P)`-algebras compatible with `P` is an isomorphism of
`κ(P)`-algebras, the residue map `P → κ(P)` being surjective. -/
private noncomputable def algEquivResidueField {P : Type*} [CommRing P] [IsLocalRing P]
    {X Y : Type*} [CommRing X] [CommRing Y] [Algebra P X] [Algebra P Y]
    [Algebra (ResidueField P) X] [Algebra (ResidueField P) Y]
    [IsScalarTower P (ResidueField P) X] [IsScalarTower P (ResidueField P) Y]
    (e : X ≃ₐ[P] Y) : X ≃ₐ[ResidueField P] Y :=
  AlgEquiv.ofRingEquiv (f := e.toRingEquiv) fun c => by
    obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := IsLocalRing.residue_surjective c
    rw [← IsLocalRing.ResidueField.algebraMap_eq,
      ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply P (ResidueField P) X,
      ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply P (ResidueField P) Y]
    exact e.commutes x

/-! ### Stacks 00SF at the fibre -/

/-- **Stacks 00SF at the fibre of `q`.**  Let `I ⊆ q` be an ideal of `B` with `B ⧸ I` syntomic
over `A`, let `p = A ∩ q`, let `P` be a local model of `A_p` and `T` one of `B_q`, and suppose the
fibre `T/𝔪_P T` is a regular local ring.  Then the ideal cut out by `I` in that fibre is generated
by a regular sequence. -/
private lemma exists_isRegular_ofList_eq_map_maximalIdeal {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [Algebra A B] [Algebra.EssFiniteType A B] (p : Ideal A) [p.IsPrime] (q : Ideal B)
    [q.IsPrime] (hpq : q.comap (algebraMap A B) = p) (I : Ideal B) (hIq : I ≤ q)
    [Algebra.Syntomic A (B ⧸ I)] (P : Type u) [CommRing P] [IsLocalRing P] [Algebra A P]
    [IsLocalization.AtPrime P p] (T : Type u) [CommRing T] [Algebra A T] [Algebra B T]
    [IsScalarTower A B T] [IsLocalization.AtPrime T q] [Algebra P T] [IsScalarTower A P T]
    (hregT : IsRegularLocalRing (T ⧸ (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T))) :
    ∃ rs : List (T ⧸ (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T)),
      IsRegular (T ⧸ (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T)) rs ∧
        Ideal.ofList rs = I.map (algebraMap B (T ⧸ (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T))) := by
  classical
  have : q.LiesOver p := ⟨hpq.symm⟩
  have hregT := hregT
  have hlocT : IsLocalRing T := IsLocalization.AtPrime.isLocalRing T q
  -- the prime `q'` of `B ⧸ I` corresponding to `q`
  have hq'p : (q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)).IsPrime :=
    Ideal.map_isPrime_of_surjective Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (by rw [Ideal.mk_ker]; exact hIq)
  have hq'q : (q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)).LiesOver q :=
    ⟨.trans (by simpa [← RingHom.ker_eq_comap_bot] using hIq)
      (Ideal.comap_map_of_surjective _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective _).symm⟩
  have : (q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)).LiesOver p :=
    Ideal.LiesOver.trans (q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) q p
  -- `T ⧸ I T` is an abstract localization of `B ⧸ I` at `q'`
  have : IsLocalization (q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)).primeCompl (T ⧸ I.map (algebraMap B T)) :=
    Ideal.algebraMapSubmonoid_primeCompl_of_liesOver_surjective
      (q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) q Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective ▸ inferInstance
  have : IsScalarTower A (B ⧸ I) (T ⧸ I.map (algebraMap B T)) :=
    .of_algebraMap_eq fun a => by
      show Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (algebraMap A T a) =
        Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (algebraMap B T (algebraMap A B a))
      rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A B T]
  -- the fibre of `B ⧸ I` at `q'` is a complete intersection over `κ(p)`
  have hci0 : IsCompleteIntersection p.ResidueField
      (p.Fiber (Localization.AtPrime (q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)))) :=
    IsCompleteIntersection.fiber_congr ((q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)).over_def p).symm
      (Algebra.Syntomic.flat_localization_and_isCompleteIntersection_fiber
        (q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))).2
  have hci1 : IsCompleteIntersection (ResidueField P)
      (ResidueField P ⊗[P] (T ⧸ I.map (algebraMap B T))) :=
    (Stacks.SyntomicLocus.isCompleteIntersection_closedFibre_iff p
      (q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) P _).mpr hci0
  -- the `κ(P)`-algebra structures on the two fibres
  let _ : Algebra (ResidueField P) (T ⧸ (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T)) :=
    inferInstanceAs (Algebra (P ⧸ maximalIdeal P) _)
  have : IsScalarTower P (ResidueField P) (T ⧸ (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T)) :=
    inferInstanceAs (IsScalarTower P (P ⧸ maximalIdeal P) _)
  have : Algebra.EssFiniteType B T := Algebra.EssFiniteType.of_isLocalization T q.primeCompl
  have : Algebra.EssFiniteType A T := Algebra.EssFiniteType.comp A B T
  have : Algebra.EssFiniteType P T := Algebra.EssFiniteType.of_comp A P T
  have : Algebra.EssFiniteType (ResidueField P)
      (T ⧸ (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T)) :=
    inferInstanceAs (Algebra.EssFiniteType (P ⧸ maximalIdeal P) _)
  let _ : Algebra (ResidueField P) ((T ⧸ I.map (algebraMap B T)) ⧸
      (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P (T ⧸ I.map (algebraMap B T)))) :=
    inferInstanceAs (Algebra (P ⧸ maximalIdeal P) _)
  have : IsScalarTower P (ResidueField P) ((T ⧸ I.map (algebraMap B T)) ⧸
      (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P (T ⧸ I.map (algebraMap B T)))) :=
    inferInstanceAs (IsScalarTower P (P ⧸ maximalIdeal P) _)
  -- `R ⧸ I R` is a complete intersection over `κ(P)`:  both it and the closed fibre of `T ⧸ I T`
  -- are `T/(I T + 𝔪_P T)`
  have hci : IsCompleteIntersection (ResidueField P)
      ((T ⧸ (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T)) ⧸
        I.map (algebraMap B (T ⧸ (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T)))) := by
    refine hci1.of_algEquiv ?_
    have e₁ : ((T ⧸ I.map (algebraMap B T)) ⧸
          (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P (T ⧸ I.map (algebraMap B T))))
            ≃ₐ[ResidueField P] ResidueField P ⊗[P] (T ⧸ I.map (algebraMap B T)) :=
      Algebra.TensorProduct.quotIdealMapEquivQuotTensor _ (maximalIdeal P)
    have e₂ : ((T ⧸ I.map (algebraMap B T)) ⧸
          (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P (T ⧸ I.map (algebraMap B T)))) ≃ₐ[P]
        ((T ⧸ I.map (algebraMap B T)) ⧸ ((maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T)).map
          (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ P (I.map (algebraMap B T)))) :=
      Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq P (map_map_mk_eq_map _ _).symm
    have e₄ : ((T ⧸ (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T)) ⧸ (I.map (algebraMap B T)).map
          (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ P ((maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T)))) ≃ₐ[P]
        ((T ⧸ (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T)) ⧸
          I.map (algebraMap B (T ⧸ (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T)))) :=
      Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq P (map_map_mk_eq_map _ _)
    exact e₁.symm.trans (algEquivResidueField (e₂.trans
      ((DoubleQuot.quotQuotEquivCommₐ P (I.map (algebraMap B T))
        ((maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T))).trans e₄)))
  -- `R ⧸ I R` is a nonzero local ring
  have hle : I.map (algebraMap B T) ⊔ (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T) ≤ maximalIdeal T := by
    refine sup_le (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun x hx =>
      (IsLocalization.AtPrime.to_map_mem_maximal_iff T q x).mpr (hIq hx)) ?_
    rw [map_maximalIdeal_eq_map_of_isLocalization p]
    refine Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun a ha => ?_
    rw [Ideal.mem_comap, IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A B T]
    refine (IsLocalization.AtPrime.to_map_mem_maximal_iff T q _).mpr ?_
    rw [← hpq] at ha
    exact ha
  have : Nontrivial ((T ⧸ (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T)) ⧸
      I.map (algebraMap B (T ⧸ (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T)))) := by
    rw [Ideal.Quotient.nontrivial_iff]
    intro htop
    have h1 : Ideal.Quotient.mk ((maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T)) 1 ∈
        Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk ((maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T)))
          (I.map (algebraMap B T)) := by
      rw [map_map_mk_eq_map, htop]
      exact Submodule.mem_top
    rw [Ideal.mem_quotient_iff_mem_sup] at h1
    exact (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal T).ne_top
      (Ideal.eq_top_of_isUnit_mem _ (hle h1) isUnit_one)
  have : IsLocalRing ((T ⧸ (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T)) ⧸
      I.map (algebraMap B (T ⧸ (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T)))) :=
    IsLocalRing.of_surjective' (Ideal.Quotient.mk _) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  -- Stacks 00SF
  have h := ((IsCompleteIntersection.tfae.{u, u, u} (ResidueField P) _).out 1 2).mp hci
  obtain ⟨rs, hreg, hker⟩ := h (T ⧸ (maximalIdeal P).map (algebraMap P T)) inferInstance
    inferInstance inferInstance inferInstance (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ (ResidueField P) _)
    Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  exact ⟨rs, hreg, by rw [hker]; exact Ideal.mk_ker⟩

/-- The conclusion of `exists_isRegular_ofList_eq_map_maximalIdeal`, transported along an equality
between the two spellings of the ideal cutting out the fibre. -/
private lemma exists_isRegular_ofList_eq_map_of_ideal_eq {B T : Type*} [CommRing B] [CommRing T]
    [Algebra B T] (I : Ideal B) {K K' : Ideal T} (h : K = K')
    (hex : ∃ rs : List (T ⧸ K), IsRegular (T ⧸ K) rs ∧
      Ideal.ofList rs = I.map (algebraMap B (T ⧸ K))) :
    ∃ rs : List (T ⧸ K'), IsRegular (T ⧸ K') rs ∧
      Ideal.ofList rs = I.map (algebraMap B (T ⧸ K')) := by
  subst h
  exact hex

/-! ### The fibre input of Stacks 063W -/

/-- **The fibre input of Stacks 063W.**  Let `A → B` be smooth, let `A → C` be syntomic, let
`φ : B → C` be a surjection of `A`-algebras and let `q` be a prime of `B` containing `I = ker φ`,
lying over `p = A ∩ q`.  Then there are `f_1, …, f_r ∈ I ∩ q` whose images in the fibre
`B_q/pB_q` form a regular sequence, and which generate `I B_q` modulo `p B_q`.

These are exactly the hypotheses on the fibre of
`Stacks.RingTheory.SpreadingOut.exists_notMem_isWeaklyRegular_and_flat_quotient_away` (Stacks
062Y (3)) and of `Stacks.RingTheory.SpreadingOut.exists_notMem_map_eq_map_away` (Stacks 062Y (2)),
whose conjunction is what Stacks 063W feeds into Stacks 067T.

The fibre `B_q/pB_q` is a regular local ring because `A → B` is smooth, and its quotient by
`I B_q` is a complete intersection over `κ(p)` because `C = B/I` is syntomic over `A`;  Stacks
00SF then generates `I B_q/pB_q` by a regular sequence, which lifts to `I` up to units. -/
theorem exists_isRegular_fibre_of_smooth_of_syntomic
    {A B C : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [CommRing C]
    [Algebra A B] [Algebra A C] [Algebra.Smooth A B] [Algebra.Syntomic A C]
    (φ : B →ₐ[A] C) (hφ : Function.Surjective φ)
    (q : Ideal B) [q.IsPrime] (hq : RingHom.ker φ ≤ q) :
    ∃ (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r → B),
      (∀ i, f i ∈ RingHom.ker φ) ∧ (∀ i, f i ∈ q) ∧
      IsRegular
        (Localization.AtPrime q ⧸
          (q.comap (algebraMap A B)).map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q)))
        (List.ofFn fun i => algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q) (f i)) ∧
      (RingHom.ker φ).map (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q)) ≤
        (Ideal.span (Set.range f)).map (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q)) ⊔
          (q.comap (algebraMap A B)).map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q)) := by
  classical
  have : Algebra.Syntomic A (B ⧸ RingHom.ker φ) :=
    Stacks.SyntomicLocus.Algebra.Syntomic.of_algEquiv
      (Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective hφ).symm
  have : q.LiesOver (q.comap (algebraMap A B)) := ⟨rfl⟩
  let _ : Algebra (Localization.AtPrime (q.comap (algebraMap A B))) (Localization.AtPrime q) :=
    Localization.AtPrime.algebraOfLiesOver (q.comap (algebraMap A B)) q
  -- Stacks 00SF at the fibre, in the spelling `p B_q`
  obtain ⟨rs, hreg, hofList⟩ := exists_isRegular_ofList_eq_map_of_ideal_eq (RingHom.ker φ)
    (map_maximalIdeal_eq_map_of_isLocalization (q.comap (algebraMap A B)))
    (exists_isRegular_ofList_eq_map_maximalIdeal (q.comap (algebraMap A B)) q rfl
      (RingHom.ker φ) hq (Localization.AtPrime (q.comap (algebraMap A B)))
      (Localization.AtPrime q)
      (isRegularLocalRing_quotient_of_smooth (q.comap (algebraMap A B)) q rfl _
        (map_maximalIdeal_eq_map_of_isLocalization (q.comap (algebraMap A B))).symm))
  have hfrac : ∀ c : Localization.AtPrime q ⧸
      (q.comap (algebraMap A B)).map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q)),
      ∃ s ∈ q.primeCompl, ∃ b : B, algebraMap B _ s * c = algebraMap B _ b := by
    intro c
    obtain ⟨t, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective c
    obtain ⟨⟨b, s⟩, hbs⟩ := IsLocalization.surj q.primeCompl t
    refine ⟨s, s.2, b, ?_⟩
    have hb := congrArg (Ideal.Quotient.mk
      ((q.comap (algebraMap A B)).map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q)))) hbs
    rw [map_mul] at hb
    rw [show algebraMap B _ (s : B)
        = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q) (s : B)) from rfl,
      show algebraMap B _ b
        = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q) b) from rfl, ← hb]
    ring
  -- lift the sequence to `ker φ`
  have key : ∀ i : Fin rs.length, ∃ s ∈ q.primeCompl, ∃ b ∈ RingHom.ker φ,
      algebraMap B _ b = algebraMap B _ s * rs.get i := by
    intro i
    refine exists_mem_of_mem_map q (RingHom.ker φ) hfrac ?_
    rw [← hofList]
    exact Ideal.subset_span (List.get_mem rs i)
  choose s hs f hf hfeq using key
  have hunit : ∀ i, IsUnit (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q ⧸
      (q.comap (algebraMap A B)).map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q))) (s i)) :=
    fun i => (IsLocalization.map_units (M := q.primeCompl) (Localization.AtPrime q)
      ⟨s i, hs i⟩).map (algebraMap (Localization.AtPrime q) _)
  have hcomp : (List.ofFn fun i : Fin rs.length => algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q ⧸
        (q.comap (algebraMap A B)).map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q))) (f i))
      = (List.ofFn fun i : Fin rs.length =>
          algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q) (f i)).map
        (algebraMap (Localization.AtPrime q) (Localization.AtPrime q ⧸
          (q.comap (algebraMap A B)).map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q)))) := by
    rw [List.map_ofFn]
    exact congrArg List.ofFn (funext fun i =>
      IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply B (Localization.AtPrime q) _ (f i))
  refine ⟨rs.length, f, hf, fun i => hq (hf i), ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [← isRegular_map_algebraMap_iff (Localization.AtPrime q ⧸
      (q.comap (algebraMap A B)).map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q))), ← hcomp]
    refine isRegular_of_forall₂_unit_mul (rs := rs) ?_ hreg
    refine List.forall₂_iff_get.mpr ⟨by simp, fun i h₁ h₂ => ?_⟩
    refine ⟨(hunit ⟨i, h₂⟩).unit, ?_⟩
    rw [List.get_ofFn]
    simpa using hfeq ⟨i, h₂⟩
  · refine Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun x hx => ?_
    rw [Ideal.mem_comap, ← Ideal.mem_quotient_iff_mem_sup, map_map_mk_eq_map]
    have hrsle : Ideal.ofList rs ≤ (Ideal.span (Set.range f)).map
        (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q ⧸
          (q.comap (algebraMap A B)).map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q)))) := by
      refine Ideal.span_le.mpr fun y hy => ?_
      obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := List.mem_iff_get.mp hy
      refine (Ideal.unit_mul_mem_iff_mem _ (hunit i)).mp ?_
      rw [← hfeq i]
      exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ (Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩)
    refine hrsle ?_
    rw [hofList]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hx

end Stacks.RingTheory.SpreadingOut

